{
  "id": "ss.relic.cocoon",
  "name": "Cocoon",
  "description": "A spindle of pale silk, tilted, with its thread still visible: five diagonal wraps drawn as darker lines across it, spaced unevenly, and one loose end come off the bottom tip and drifting away in a lazy S. The wraps are what make it silk and not a seed or a drop — a smooth pale spindle read as a grain — and the trailing thread says it was spun rather than grown, which is the relic: six seconds without a hit spins a shell that eats the next one. Pointed at both ends so it cannot be the round-bottomed drop of ss.relic.coldblood, and left plain of any split or glow so it stays the shut case where ss.relic.chrysalis is the opened one. The loose end was first drawn as a tight curl and read as a hook.",
